1
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:15,889
Your daughter is 4 now, right?

2
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:16,850
Yes.

3
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:20,437
She doesn't react
even when her mother talks to her?

4
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:22,521
My wife...

5
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:25,692
Passed away when she was 1.

6
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:32,198
Minami.

7
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:34,909
Minami.

8
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,662
Minami Minamida.

9
00:00:44,794 --> 00:00:47,046
It's great that you got a toy.

10
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:48,965
Do you like it?

11
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:51,718
Hey, Minami.

12
00:00:53,052 --> 00:00:55,638
Do you know who Dad is?

13
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:16,659
<i>My name is Minami Minamida.</i>

14
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:20,371
<i>Read forwards or backwards,
it's Minami Minamida.</i>

15
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:24,542
<i>Kayak, deed, rotator, civic, racecar,
Minami Minamida.</i>

16
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:47,482
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR NEW JOB

17
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:59,452
MINAMI'S DAD
MAKOTO MINAMIDA

18
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:02,412
Good morning.

19
00:02:02,413 --> 00:02:03,498
Morning.

20
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:09,628
<i>It will be sunny over a wide area today,
perfect for going out.</i>

21
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:13,298
<i>Tokyo's estimated high is 21 degrees.</i>

22
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:16,761
<i>The estimated low is 17 degrees. Perf--</i>

23
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:19,721
The estimated high is 21 degrees.

24
00:02:19,722 --> 00:02:22,016
The estimated low is 17 degrees.

25
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:26,521
Minami, it looks good on you.

26
00:02:31,025 --> 00:02:33,277
That's your gift from Dad
for your new job.

27
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:34,320
How is it? Happy?

28
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:37,698
I'm very happy.

29
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:39,659
Minami, no.

30
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:46,124
Here.

31
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:50,419
This is the "happy" face.

32
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:52,547
HAPPY

33
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:56,467
Like this?

34
00:02:57,051 --> 00:02:59,262
Yes! You look happy.

35
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:04,726
Here is the Minami Minamida set.
Here you go.

36
00:03:07,103 --> 00:03:08,104
Let's eat.

37
00:03:18,948 --> 00:03:21,618
<i>I always eat salted rice balls
for my meals.</i>

38
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:24,202
<i>Salted rice balls are safe.</i>

39
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:26,830
<i>Since they only contain salt and rice,</i>

40
00:03:26,831 --> 00:03:29,167
<i>I'm not surprised by unexpected flavors.</i>

41
00:03:31,961 --> 00:03:33,046
Listen, Minami.

42
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:35,839
No parroting at work.

43
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,218
And don't say anything unnecessary
in your introduction.

44
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:40,720
Don't be too honest, either.

45
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:45,058
Echolalia, needless details,
and total honesty are forbidden.

46
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:46,851
And whatever you do,

47
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:49,020
don't talk about whales.

48
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:54,107
What if we need to talk about whales?

49
00:03:54,108 --> 00:03:56,402
Is your workplace Kamogawa Sea World?

50
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:58,820
That'll never come up.

51
00:03:58,821 --> 00:04:01,365
But what if it becomes
absolutely necessary,

52
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:04,369
and everyone except me
is talking about nothing but whales?

53
00:04:05,536 --> 00:04:07,996
Then it's fine.

54
00:04:07,997 --> 00:04:09,165
Okay!

55
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:13,503
Thank you for the meal.

56
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,256
Are you leaving already?

57
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:18,841
Your lunch box is in your bag.

58
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:20,843
Thank you.

59
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:27,849
I'll be going now.

60
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:28,810
Take care.

61
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:31,229
Eat your side dishes, too.

62
00:04:44,742 --> 00:04:46,451
AN AUTISTIC ATTORNEY IS BORN!

63
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:49,079
HIROKAWA & HOWARD LPC
MINAMI MINAMIDA

64
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,499
HER FATHER MAKOTO,
ALWAYS BY HER SIDE

65
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:04,262
<i>I don't like the morning commute
because there are too many people.</i>

66
00:05:08,057 --> 00:05:09,308
<i>At times like this,</i>

67
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:12,228
<i>I try to imagine whales
swimming freely in the ocean.</i>

68
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:33,124
<i>Whales are fascinating.</i>

69
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:37,085
<i>They're said to sense
the earth's magnetic field,</i>

70
00:05:37,086 --> 00:05:39,588
<i>and can migrate thousands of miles</i>

71
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:43,301
<i>in that vast ocean without getting lost.</i>

72
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:50,849
<i>What awaits me</i>

73
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,685
<i>as I sail this ocean?</i>

74
00:06:23,216 --> 00:06:24,842
ELEVATOR UNDER CONSTRUCTION

75
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,464
Excuse me.

76
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:09,345
I'm sorry.

77
00:07:18,604 --> 00:07:19,896
PARALEGAL MINATO FUNAI

78
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:21,732
Shall I show you to the stairs?

79
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:27,154
It's a bit hard to find your way
to the reception

80
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:29,365
from the emergency stairs
in this building.

81
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:31,868
Where are you headed?

82
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,662
Hirokawa & Howard LPC.

83
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:37,122
Then we're on the same floor.

84
00:07:37,123 --> 00:07:39,166
Do you have an appointment with someone?

85
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,043
I have an appointment with Mr. Miyaji.

86
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:43,171
Good morning.

87
00:07:44,255 --> 00:07:47,258
HIROKAWA & HOWARD LPC

88
00:07:54,932 --> 00:07:57,434
Here it is. Mr. Miyaji's office.

89
00:07:57,435 --> 00:07:59,019
Well, I'll leave you here.

90
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,521
Thank you very much.

91
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:02,440
You're welcome.

92
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:12,158
Come in.

93
00:08:13,242 --> 00:08:14,327
Excuse me.

94
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:28,673
ATTORNEY
KOHARU ASAHI

95
00:08:28,674 --> 00:08:30,343
May I ask who you are?

96
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:33,428
I'm Minami Minamida,
and I'll be working here

97
00:08:33,429 --> 00:08:35,222
as an attorney starting today.

98
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:36,139
PARTNER
KENGO MIYAJI

99
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,349
Is it that time already?

100
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:38,266
ATTORNEY
TAKUMA HIMI

101
00:08:38,267 --> 00:08:39,476
A new hire right now?

102
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:41,187
She's six months behind you two.

103
00:08:42,104 --> 00:08:44,397
RESUME
MINAMI MINAMIDA

104
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:47,651
Well, she graduated top of her class
from Tokyo University,

105
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:50,738
and ranked first in the bar exam.

106
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:53,491
You're quite outstanding.

107
00:08:53,991 --> 00:08:56,369
Have you seen the second page
of my resume?

108
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:02,624
I wrote Autism Spectrum Disorder
on the second page.

109
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,000
Autism Spectrum Disorder?

110
00:09:04,001 --> 00:09:06,836
Autism Spectrum Disorder
is a developmental disorder.

111
00:09:06,837 --> 00:09:08,296
Due to atypical brain function,

112
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:09,756
social communication

113
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:11,049
can be difficult--

114
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:12,301
I know what it is.

115
00:09:13,177 --> 00:09:14,719
I see.

116
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,347
Any other special notes?

117
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:18,181
What?

118
00:09:18,182 --> 00:09:21,601
Read forwards or backwards,
my name is Minami Minamida.

119
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:24,564
Kayak, deed, rotator, civic, racecar,
Minami Minamida.

120
00:09:28,859 --> 00:09:31,111
Wait, it's today, right?
You know, that thing.

121
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:33,363
I need to go for a bit. I'm sorry,

122
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:35,740
but could you two handle
the greetings and stuff?

123
00:09:35,741 --> 00:09:36,784
What?

124
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:42,455
Ms. Minamida, you can't do that at work.

125
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:45,625
The instructors warned you
about the kayak and racecar stuff.

126
00:09:45,626 --> 00:09:49,129
I can't do that at work.
Kayaks and racecars are forbidden.

127
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:51,006
But I can't help but say them.

128
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:53,758
What? Ms. Asahi, do you know her?

129
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:55,678
We were legal trainees together.

130
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:58,097
Look, you have bedhead again.

131
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:03,227
I'm surprised you got in.
How did you get in?

132
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:05,103
The same as everyone else.

133
00:10:05,104 --> 00:10:06,939
Through the automatic front doors.

134
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:11,151
PARTNER
NAGISA HIROKAWA

135
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:12,153
Come in.

136
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,531
Mr. Miyaji is here.

137
00:10:16,532 --> 00:10:17,867
SECRETARY
KAEDE TSUCHIMURA

138
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:22,579
The rookie you hired has arrived.

139
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:23,496
I see.

140
00:10:23,497 --> 00:10:26,333
There's a second page to this resume.

141
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:28,252
It says she has autism.

142
00:10:28,836 --> 00:10:29,712
Yes.

143
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:31,922
Why hire her knowing...

144
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:34,258
Her background isn't bad.

145
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,885
Doesn't she just have a good memory?

146
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:39,387
I don't think someone
who can't introduce herself properly

147
00:10:39,388 --> 00:10:40,972
is fit for the job.

148
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:42,266
Then, maybe,

149
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:45,560
I should ask my father
about how excellent you were

150
00:10:45,561 --> 00:10:46,978
when you were a rookie.

151
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:47,938
That's...

152
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:51,734
Understood.

153
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:54,152
If you say so,

154
00:10:54,153 --> 00:10:56,238
I'll entrust her with one case.

155
00:10:56,739 --> 00:10:59,949
If she isn't at the level
to stand in court,

156
00:10:59,950 --> 00:11:01,869
will you reconsider her employment?

157
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:03,621
Yes.

158
00:11:04,413 --> 00:11:05,246
Fair enough.

159
00:11:05,247 --> 00:11:06,290
Excuse me then.

160
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,636
MINAMIDA, BORN DEC. 20, 2002 (23)
4-4-1 MIDORIGAOKA, NAKANO, TOKYO

161
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:22,222
Well then, let's start the meeting.

162
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:25,350
This time, I'm thinking
of having you handle a criminal case

163
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:27,561
instead of a civil one...

164
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:30,314
Ms. Minamida.

165
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:31,815
Yes.

166
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:33,359
Can I ask you something?

167
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:36,153
Why did you become a lawyer?

168
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:41,033
Because I passed the bar exam.
Is it different for you, Mr. Miyaji?

169
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:43,869
I'm asking
about your reason or motivation.

170
00:11:45,079 --> 00:11:46,080
Motivation?

171
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:51,627
Never mind.

172
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:55,131
The defendant is a 72-year-old woman.

173
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:59,134
She was caring for her husband
because he had dementia,

174
00:11:59,135 --> 00:12:01,011
but they got into a fight that day.

175
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:05,558
Angered by his insults, she hit his head.

176
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:09,144
Yes, that's right,
with the iron that was nearby.

177
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:10,521
With the nearby iron.

178
00:12:17,319 --> 00:12:20,113
This iron looks just like a sperm whale.

179
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:21,699
A sperm whale?

180
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:25,326
Yes. Their spermaceti organ
holds wax-like liquid

181
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:27,745
to produce sound waves.

182
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:29,164
Yes, I understand.

183
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:30,206
- Moving on--
- Have you

184
00:12:30,207 --> 00:12:31,916
seen the animated film <i>Pinocchio?</i>

185
00:12:31,917 --> 00:12:33,626
The whale that appears in the climax

186
00:12:33,627 --> 00:12:35,086
is modeled after a sperm whale

187
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:36,880
due to its square-shaped head,

188
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:38,089
but real sperm whales

189
00:12:38,090 --> 00:12:39,883
have hidden teeth in their upper jaw--

190
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:42,219
- What is this about?
- Sperm whales.

191
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:45,931
Please focus.

192
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:47,933
I'm sorry.

193
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:50,519
Whale talk is forbidden.

194
00:12:56,609 --> 00:12:59,068
Hey, a package arrived.

195
00:12:59,069 --> 00:13:00,154
You sign for it.

196
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:04,742
The least you could do is grab it.

197
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:09,454
Thanks for your hard work.

198
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:10,955
- A signature, right?
- Thank you.

199
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:12,207
Can you put it here?

200
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:13,374
Sure.

201
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:16,086
- Wasn't it heavy?
- No, not at all.

202
00:13:16,712 --> 00:13:17,796
Thanks a lot.

203
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:19,464
Anytime.

204
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:23,218
You're nice and seem earnest.

205
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:24,887
You'd make a good husband.

206
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:27,180
Seriously, what the hell?

207
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:30,100
Flirting with another man
in the middle of the day!

208
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:31,852
Please don't mind him.

209
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:34,229
Thanks for the delivery.

210
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,439
Thank you.

211
00:13:37,566 --> 00:13:38,567
Have a good day.

212
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:45,699
Stop it.

213
00:13:46,283 --> 00:13:47,742
He could be my grandson.

214
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:50,828
You have a husband,
yet you flirt with other men.

215
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:52,038
Don't say that.

216
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:55,876
You're just hoping I die soon!

217
00:14:02,132 --> 00:14:03,676
Why would you do that?

218
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,760
I'm the one who has to clean it up!

219
00:14:05,761 --> 00:14:07,428
Don't act all high and mighty

220
00:14:07,429 --> 00:14:09,306
just because you clean.

221
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:12,810
I can't take this anymore.

222
00:14:15,437 --> 00:14:16,271
What?

223
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:17,481
Let's die.

224
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,442
Let's die together...

225
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:22,861
And end this!

226
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:24,280
Stop! Stop!

227
00:14:25,614 --> 00:14:27,324
I'll kill you...

228
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:30,118
And then I'll die too!

229
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:32,204
This is the end.

230
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:41,713
Dear?

231
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:42,756
No!

232
00:14:44,675 --> 00:14:45,717
Wake up!

233
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,844
<i>Wake up, dear!</i>

234
00:14:47,845 --> 00:14:48,803
KEIKO ICHINOSE

235
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:51,639
The husband suffered a subdural hematoma
with a 12-week recovery.

236
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:54,684
Wife charged with attempted murder.

237
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:56,437
H-- Hey...

238
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:58,564
Why are you repeating me?

239
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:01,816
I'm sorry.

240
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:03,484
Echolalia is forbidden!

241
00:15:03,485 --> 00:15:04,612
Echolalia?

242
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:07,363
It means parroting words.

243
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:09,074
It's a trait of autism.

244
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:13,037
Let's drop the echolalia then.

245
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:16,789
Anyway...

246
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:18,416
Wife charged with attempted murder.

247
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:20,628
But fortunately,
no request for detention was made.

248
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:22,921
Even though it's attempted murder?

249
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:25,131
The prosecution is sympathetic, too.

250
00:15:25,132 --> 00:15:26,799
The defendant herself is in her 70s,

251
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:30,012
yet she's been caring
for her husband in his 80s with dementia.

252
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:32,222
Now,

253
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:37,227
Ms. Minamida, what should you do
for this defendant?

254
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:40,980
Get her a suspended sentence.

255
00:15:40,981 --> 00:15:44,068
Despite the charge,
it's very possible here.

256
00:15:50,491 --> 00:15:52,326
Hello. I'm Minami Minamida.

257
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:54,328
I will do my absolute best!

258
00:15:57,122 --> 00:15:58,123
What about you?

259
00:15:58,749 --> 00:16:01,961
I will be defending you as well,
of course, but she will be in charge.

260
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:07,257
I was very surprised
when I looked at the files.

261
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,259
I lived there until 19 years ago, too.

262
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:11,762
In that apartment in Nishikasai.

263
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:15,182
Ocean Heim Nishikasai, Unit 202.

264
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:18,685
It's the unit right next to yours,
Ms. Ichinose.

265
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:19,602
Really?

266
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:21,771
I remembered the name of the building.

267
00:16:21,772 --> 00:16:23,940
Read forwards or backwards,

268
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:27,276
202 and the kanji for Nishikasai
read the same.

269
00:16:27,277 --> 00:16:28,194
MINAMI MINAMIDA

270
00:16:28,195 --> 00:16:29,697
Minami Minamida...

271
00:16:31,115 --> 00:16:32,824
Are you that Little Minami?

272
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:34,493
Do you know her?

273
00:16:35,911 --> 00:16:41,374
Little Minami really became a lawyer!

274
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:43,377
Isn't that amazing?

275
00:16:44,878 --> 00:16:46,295
Well, I'm going to head out.

276
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:48,465
You can hear the rest directly from her.

277
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:50,133
I'll take my leave.

278
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:55,054
It's truly amazing.
You worked so hard, Minami!

279
00:16:55,055 --> 00:16:58,142
STATEMENT OF PLANNED DEFENSE

280
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:04,063
What is this?

281
00:17:04,064 --> 00:17:06,232
It's the defense's
planned defense statement.

282
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:07,233
I know that.

283
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:08,818
But it says "not guilty" here?

284
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:11,989
I intend to plead not guilty
to the charge of attempted murder.

285
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,824
No matter how big our firm is,

286
00:17:14,825 --> 00:17:16,451
there are things we can and cannot do.

287
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:18,911
But she should be found not guilty
of attempted murder.

288
00:17:18,912 --> 00:17:20,371
I told you, didn't I?

289
00:17:20,372 --> 00:17:23,207
Get a suspended sentence,
which is fine for this case.

290
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:25,001
But that's not good enough.

291
00:17:25,002 --> 00:17:26,170
Why not?

292
00:17:27,838 --> 00:17:29,505
This case is interesting.

293
00:17:29,506 --> 00:17:31,507
It's like one of my favorite
whale riddles.

294
00:17:31,508 --> 00:17:34,052
- Excuse me?
- When a 22-ton sperm whale

295
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,720
eats a 500-kilogram giant squid

296
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:38,264
and lays a 1.3-ton egg six hours later,

297
00:17:38,265 --> 00:17:40,391
how many tons does the sperm whale weigh?

298
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:41,309
I have no idea.

299
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:44,312
The correct answer is,
"Whales don't lay eggs."

300
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:46,773
If you focus on the weight,
you can't find the answer.

301
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:47,690
You'll miss it.

302
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:48,900
And?

303
00:17:48,901 --> 00:17:49,817
This case

304
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:53,029
is a criminal case, so people
tend to focus on criminal law.

305
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,781
But that won't give you the answer.

306
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:56,449
The answer is in civil law.

307
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:59,660
- Civil law?
- Civil Code Article 891, Item 1 stipulates

308
00:17:59,661 --> 00:18:01,412
that you cannot inherit

309
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:03,706
the assets of someone you tried to kill.

310
00:18:03,707 --> 00:18:04,791
Inheritance...

311
00:18:04,792 --> 00:18:08,211
The defendant currently lives
mainly off her husband's pension.

312
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:10,588
If she's found guilty of attempted murder,

313
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:13,925
she may lose his pension

314
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:16,636
and inheritance after he passes,

315
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:18,221
leaving her destitute.

316
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:20,306
Therefore, I will get her
a suspended sentence

317
00:18:20,307 --> 00:18:22,392
for bodily injury, not attempted murder.

318
00:18:28,148 --> 00:18:30,817
Were you testing her to see
if she'd notice

319
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:32,485
the hidden issue in this case?

320
00:18:32,486 --> 00:18:33,403
No.

321
00:18:34,154 --> 00:18:35,656
I hadn't noticed it.

322
00:18:36,323 --> 00:18:38,492
There was a hint in her statement.

323
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:41,327
On page 24, line 7, it says,

324
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:44,372
"Five years ago,
I quit my part-time cleaning job

325
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:46,958
to focus on caring for my husband."

326
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:48,376
That's what it says.

327
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:49,836
Remembering that,

328
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:51,546
I checked her finances.

329
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:52,547
QUIT MY PART-TIME JOB

330
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:54,340
Ms. Minamida, that's brilliant.

331
00:18:54,341 --> 00:18:57,469
Even a normal lawyer
wouldn't easily catch that.

332
00:19:02,015 --> 00:19:02,849
What is it?

333
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:04,101
I'm sorry.

334
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:08,981
Saying "normal lawyer" was rude.

335
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:13,860
Please don't worry about it.

336
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:16,155
Because I'm not a normal lawyer.

337
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:20,701
Who exactly is Ms. Minamida?

338
00:19:21,410 --> 00:19:23,620
Why did the Managing Partner hire her now?

339
00:19:24,913 --> 00:19:25,830
Beats me.

340
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:28,207
Was she like that
during the legal training too?

341
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:30,085
Do you want to hear about it?

342
00:19:30,794 --> 00:19:32,336
Like the time she finished

343
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:34,214
a group assignment all by herself.

344
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:38,134
Or the time she corrected
the documents our instructor

345
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:40,219
was submitting to the court.

346
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,890
Those are quite amusing memories.

347
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:46,143
Being with her makes me feel useless.

348
00:19:47,811 --> 00:19:50,354
I try to help her
because I think she's in danger,

349
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:52,608
but in the end, she wins and I lose.

350
00:19:53,734 --> 00:19:56,028
Never thought it'd be the same at work.

351
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:59,990
I don't think
she's much of a rival, though.

352
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:05,579
Speak of the devil.

353
00:20:06,705 --> 00:20:08,832
She is bad with escalators.

354
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:12,586
What should we do? Help her?

355
00:20:17,174 --> 00:20:19,009
I have a meeting with a client.

356
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:34,024
The stairs are over there.

357
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:36,193
I know.

358
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:38,153
I see.

359
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:46,870
I'm waiting for someone.

360
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,917
Couldn't you get on the escalator

361
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:54,962
if you just catch the timing?

362
00:20:57,297 --> 00:20:59,841
Try catching the rhythm.

363
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:10,143
Give it a try next time.

364
00:21:12,938 --> 00:21:14,314
I need to make a call.

365
00:21:30,247 --> 00:21:31,415
Hello.

366
00:21:31,915 --> 00:21:33,208
Hello.

367
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:40,298
I was told to guide the attorney
to the hospital.

368
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:42,801
I was told to wait for someone
to guide me to the hospital.

369
00:21:43,635 --> 00:21:45,971
I apologize. You are the attorney.

370
00:21:47,472 --> 00:21:48,849
I'm Minami Minamida.

371
00:21:50,475 --> 00:21:52,394
Minami Minamida.

372
00:21:53,228 --> 00:21:54,688
I'm Funai, a paralegal.

373
00:21:55,272 --> 00:21:56,773
Well, shall we go?

374
00:22:00,193 --> 00:22:01,278
Want to try?

375
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,575
Do you think I can?

376
00:22:07,159 --> 00:22:08,618
Please copy me.

377
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:28,096
Exactly.

378
00:22:28,930 --> 00:22:29,931
Let's try it.

379
00:22:41,026 --> 00:22:42,194
Now!

380
00:22:54,414 --> 00:22:55,373
You did it! See?

381
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:57,584
Yes.

382
00:22:58,168 --> 00:22:59,419
I did it!

383
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:09,596
It feels like I'm diving deep
into the bottom of the ocean!

384
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:44,798
When getting off...

385
00:23:58,103 --> 00:23:58,979
Now.

386
00:24:01,731 --> 00:24:03,232
I did it!

387
00:24:03,233 --> 00:24:04,693
There you go!

388
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:11,199
They look ridiculous.

389
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:17,205
Under the dura mater here.

390
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:19,457
What looks white is blood.

391
00:24:20,834 --> 00:24:23,545
Subdural hematomas
are mainly caused by injuries.

392
00:24:25,589 --> 00:24:26,630
This is it, right?

393
00:24:26,631 --> 00:24:27,674
ISAO ICHINOSE

394
00:24:34,431 --> 00:24:35,599
Is something wrong?

395
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:38,935
Sudden environment changes confuse me.

396
00:24:53,491 --> 00:24:54,743
He's sleeping right now.

397
00:24:55,368 --> 00:24:56,620
Shall we talk outside?

398
00:24:58,246 --> 00:24:59,079
Who is it?

399
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:00,540
You're awake?

400
00:25:01,124 --> 00:25:02,583
Can you come over here?

401
00:25:02,584 --> 00:25:05,378
Honey, do you remember her?

402
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:09,132
Little Minami
who used to live in Unit 202.

403
00:25:09,758 --> 00:25:13,261
You know, her dad was at the
University of Tokyo's law school.

404
00:25:13,970 --> 00:25:16,473
Minami is a lawyer now.

405
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:21,852
Hello.

406
00:25:21,853 --> 00:25:24,105
I came to speak with you today.

407
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:30,486
Also, could you sign this petition
requesting leniency

408
00:25:30,487 --> 00:25:31,947
for the defendant?

409
00:25:33,907 --> 00:25:37,577
Are you that pervy four-eyes' daughter?

410
00:25:38,078 --> 00:25:38,911
Pervy four-eyes?

411
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:40,621
Why are you here?

412
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:41,997
And you, don't tell me...

413
00:25:41,998 --> 00:25:44,833
Are you still seeing that pervy four-eyes?

414
00:25:44,834 --> 00:25:46,878
- Hey, don't say weird things--
- Get out!

415
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:49,256
Your old man is that pervy four-eyes.

416
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:53,217
He made a move on my wife while I was out!

417
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:54,468
Stop it already!

418
00:25:54,469 --> 00:25:55,469
Please calm down!

419
00:25:55,470 --> 00:25:57,389
- She is defending your wife.
- Shut up!

420
00:25:58,348 --> 00:25:59,723
You bowl cut!

421
00:25:59,724 --> 00:26:02,435
Don't you ever show your face to me again!

422
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:05,563
You hear me? Don't ever come back!

423
00:26:06,523 --> 00:26:08,984
Tell that to that pervy four-eyes, too!

424
00:26:17,158 --> 00:26:18,118
I'm sorry.

425
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:25,250
My husband's always been paranoid.

426
00:26:27,252 --> 00:26:30,672
It has gotten worse
since he developed dementia.

427
00:26:31,715 --> 00:26:34,009
If I have to see him like this,

428
00:26:34,592 --> 00:26:36,469
I should've just killed him then.

429
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:40,639
Then, was your statement to the police

430
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:43,935
that you wanted to kill your husband
your true intention?

431
00:26:45,395 --> 00:26:48,105
Right now, yes. It is my true intention.

432
00:26:48,106 --> 00:26:49,565
What matters

433
00:26:49,566 --> 00:26:51,359
is how you felt then, not now.

434
00:26:53,653 --> 00:26:55,947
I don't know what to say.

435
00:26:56,948 --> 00:26:58,992
The law heavily weighs your feelings.

436
00:26:59,826 --> 00:27:02,036
Intending to kill means attempted murder.

437
00:27:02,037 --> 00:27:04,288
Intending to injure is assault.

438
00:27:04,289 --> 00:27:06,499
An accident is accidental injury.

439
00:27:08,001 --> 00:27:09,878
The charge changes based on your feelings.

440
00:27:14,007 --> 00:27:16,259
Human feelings are really difficult.

441
00:27:17,761 --> 00:27:19,219
I was taught

442
00:27:19,220 --> 00:27:22,431
that selfless acts
are acts of compassion and love.

443
00:27:22,432 --> 00:27:23,932
Closing the blinds

444
00:27:23,933 --> 00:27:26,685
so it isn't too bright
for someone sleeping

445
00:27:26,686 --> 00:27:28,145
is a selfless act.

446
00:27:28,146 --> 00:27:30,815
You don't do that
for someone you want to kill.

447
00:27:33,818 --> 00:27:34,778
Am I wrong?

448
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:47,457
CREATIVE RICE BALLS
BEAMS

449
00:27:51,795 --> 00:27:54,255
MINAMI'S BEST FRIEND
RIRII MADOKA

450
00:27:57,092 --> 00:27:58,175
I'm home.

451
00:27:58,176 --> 00:27:59,468
Welcome back.

452
00:27:59,469 --> 00:28:01,346
Minami!

453
00:28:02,597 --> 00:28:03,722
<i>Minami to the Minamida</i>

454
00:28:03,723 --> 00:28:05,225
<i>Ririi to the Madoka</i>

455
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:10,687
My best friend had her first day at work,

456
00:28:10,688 --> 00:28:12,689
so I came to check on you!

457
00:28:12,690 --> 00:28:14,233
Thank you, Ririi.

458
00:28:14,234 --> 00:28:18,279
Can't believe you're braving
the real world now.

459
00:28:18,947 --> 00:28:22,032
I need to hurry
and make a living from my art, too.

460
00:28:22,033 --> 00:28:23,659
I like your art, Ririi.

461
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:26,120
Until you can make a living,
you can eat rice balls here.

462
00:28:26,121 --> 00:28:29,039
Here's the new tropical rice ball.

463
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:31,333
For Minami, the Minami Minamida set.

464
00:28:31,334 --> 00:28:33,253
- Thanks, Mr. Minamida!
- Here you go.

465
00:28:34,754 --> 00:28:36,172
- Let's eat.
- Let's eat.

466
00:28:38,383 --> 00:28:39,384
By the way, Dad.

467
00:28:40,593 --> 00:28:42,302
Are you pervy four-eyes?

468
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:44,346
What's this all of a sudden?

469
00:28:44,347 --> 00:28:46,516
Ms. Ichinose's husband said that.

470
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:48,226
Ms. Ichinose?

471
00:28:48,852 --> 00:28:52,020
Of Unit 201 at Ocean Heim Nishikasai.

472
00:28:52,021 --> 00:28:53,272
That one?

473
00:28:53,273 --> 00:28:55,315
That you hit on his wife while he was out.

474
00:28:55,316 --> 00:28:57,025
No, I didn't.

475
00:28:57,026 --> 00:28:59,237
Her husband was just--

476
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:02,365
Wait, how do you know her?

477
00:29:03,241 --> 00:29:04,367
That...

478
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:06,703
I can't say due to confidentiality.

479
00:29:08,705 --> 00:29:10,748
Ririi, I have a trial coming up.

480
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:13,083
A jury trial.
I'll be arguing in front of everyone.

481
00:29:13,084 --> 00:29:14,501
That's awesome.

482
00:29:14,502 --> 00:29:15,586
She's having a trial?

483
00:29:15,587 --> 00:29:17,630
I can't say that either.
It's confidential.

484
00:29:18,798 --> 00:29:21,717
I know! I'll draw you arguing in court

485
00:29:21,718 --> 00:29:23,177
to celebrate.

486
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:25,180
Minami, strike a lawyer pose.

487
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:30,100
Like this?

488
00:29:30,101 --> 00:29:31,226
Nice. Give it a line.

489
00:29:31,227 --> 00:29:32,771
- A line?
- "Objection!"

490
00:29:33,730 --> 00:29:34,897
- Objection!
- Make it bigger.

491
00:29:34,898 --> 00:29:37,524
- Objection!
- Yes! Use your diaphragm!

492
00:29:37,525 --> 00:29:41,529
You are fined 100,000 yen!

493
00:29:42,781 --> 00:29:44,032
What did I do?

494
00:29:46,910 --> 00:29:48,912
COURTHOUSE

495
00:30:02,342 --> 00:30:03,342
FIRST HEARING

496
00:30:03,343 --> 00:30:05,470
Defense, your opening statement, please.

497
00:30:10,391 --> 00:30:12,434
Defense, what is the matter?

498
00:30:12,435 --> 00:30:13,686
Your opening statement.

499
00:30:15,146 --> 00:30:17,273
Ms. Minamida, the opening statement.

500
00:30:18,024 --> 00:30:19,441
What is wrong?

501
00:30:19,442 --> 00:30:20,359
Minami!

502
00:30:20,360 --> 00:30:21,485
RELAX, MINAMI!!

503
00:30:21,486 --> 00:30:22,570
Minami!

504
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:48,012
Before my opening statement,

505
00:30:49,597 --> 00:30:50,932
I would like to say one thing.

506
00:30:52,392 --> 00:30:53,309
I have

507
00:30:54,644 --> 00:30:56,980
a disability called
Autism Spectrum Disorder,

508
00:30:57,647 --> 00:30:58,940
and to you all,

509
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:02,569
my way of speaking and my actions
may seem unnatural.

510
00:31:03,236 --> 00:31:04,070
However,

511
00:31:05,655 --> 00:31:06,739
my love for the law

512
00:31:07,949 --> 00:31:10,242
and my respect for the defendant

513
00:31:10,243 --> 00:31:12,370
are no different from any other lawyer.

514
00:31:14,664 --> 00:31:15,790
As a defense attorney,

515
00:31:16,583 --> 00:31:17,917
I will do my absolute best

516
00:31:18,751 --> 00:31:21,671
to help the defendant
and reveal the truth of this case.

517
00:31:31,514 --> 00:31:32,849
Order in the court!

518
00:31:35,602 --> 00:31:38,146
You love the law, do you?

519
00:31:40,064 --> 00:31:41,065
That is a good thing.

520
00:31:45,361 --> 00:31:46,194
DEFENDANT
QUESTIONING

521
00:31:46,195 --> 00:31:48,072
"I'll kill you and then I'll die too."

522
00:31:49,407 --> 00:31:51,951
This is your statement to the police
after the incident.

523
00:31:52,577 --> 00:31:54,913
There were police officers there
at the time,

524
00:31:55,496 --> 00:31:58,374
so I got nervous and just said that.

525
00:31:59,334 --> 00:32:01,668
But I had no intention of killing him.

526
00:32:01,669 --> 00:32:03,629
Would someone
who had no intention of killing

527
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:05,839
talk about dying or ending it all?

528
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:07,174
Objection!

529
00:32:07,175 --> 00:32:09,843
Leading the witness
by assuming intent to kill.

530
00:32:09,844 --> 00:32:10,762
Sustained.

531
00:32:16,976 --> 00:32:18,937
Defense, please take your seat.

532
00:32:23,816 --> 00:32:27,612
This is the iron the defendant used
when she attacked.

533
00:32:29,113 --> 00:32:30,073
Defendant.

534
00:32:30,823 --> 00:32:32,617
You hit him on the head with this,

535
00:32:33,159 --> 00:32:35,286
yet you truly had
no intention of killing him?

536
00:32:35,912 --> 00:32:39,373
Didn't you actually want
your husband dead?

537
00:32:39,374 --> 00:32:40,666
Objection.

538
00:32:40,667 --> 00:32:41,960
Leading the witness.

539
00:32:43,127 --> 00:32:44,170
Overruled.

540
00:32:46,172 --> 00:32:48,716
Defendant, please answer the question.

541
00:32:51,427 --> 00:32:53,805
I'm sorry, Your Honor.

542
00:32:56,015 --> 00:32:58,226
I devoted myself to my husband
for so long,

543
00:32:59,227 --> 00:33:00,937
yet I was treated terribly,

544
00:33:02,939 --> 00:33:04,899
so I think I was feeling resentful.

545
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:08,319
I'm so sorry.

546
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:12,156
Please forgive me.

547
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:26,044
That prosecutor was pretty tough.

548
00:33:26,045 --> 00:33:28,797
Next time, we'll be examining
the victim as a witness.

549
00:33:28,798 --> 00:33:30,257
Then we'll have him testify

550
00:33:30,258 --> 00:33:32,300
that he doesn't want her punished.

551
00:33:32,301 --> 00:33:34,344
Will he be able to testify properly?

552
00:33:34,345 --> 00:33:35,929
He had quite a rough temper.

553
00:33:35,930 --> 00:33:38,515
The moment he saw Ms. Minamida,
he started hurling abuse.

554
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:40,476
Abuse? What did he say?

555
00:33:42,103 --> 00:33:43,562
He said, "You bowl cut."

556
00:33:43,563 --> 00:33:45,981
"Your old man is a pervy four-eyes."

557
00:33:45,982 --> 00:33:46,898
What on earth?

558
00:33:46,899 --> 00:33:50,028
He suspects that my father
and the defendant had an affair.

559
00:33:51,404 --> 00:33:53,156
That does sound difficult.

560
00:33:53,948 --> 00:33:55,532
I asked the defendant

561
00:33:55,533 --> 00:33:58,160
and got the victim to sign a petition

562
00:33:58,161 --> 00:34:00,037
requesting no severe punishment,

563
00:34:00,038 --> 00:34:01,622
but should we submit it?

564
00:34:03,708 --> 00:34:05,084
What is this, a petition?

565
00:34:06,002 --> 00:34:07,086
No, don't submit it.

566
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:10,672
I will handle the questioning,
so draft up a script.

567
00:34:10,673 --> 00:34:12,341
Yes, understood.

568
00:34:27,565 --> 00:34:30,234
SECOND HEARING: WITNESS EXAMINATION

569
00:34:34,530 --> 00:34:36,531
Defense, proceed
with the witness examination.

570
00:34:36,532 --> 00:34:37,575
Yes, Your Honor.

571
00:34:44,999 --> 00:34:46,667
Ms. Minamida, you go instead.

572
00:34:48,836 --> 00:34:50,545
Funai said so, right?

573
00:34:50,546 --> 00:34:52,756
That he hurled abuse
the moment he saw you.

574
00:34:52,757 --> 00:34:54,175
Draw the abuse out of him.

575
00:34:57,303 --> 00:34:59,763
Defense, please proceed
with the questioning.

576
00:34:59,764 --> 00:35:00,806
I am doing it now.

577
00:35:00,807 --> 00:35:01,974
Come on, hurry up.

578
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:05,478
Yes.

579
00:35:16,239 --> 00:35:17,197
Hello.

580
00:35:17,198 --> 00:35:19,492
I'm Minami Minamida, your wife's attorney.

581
00:35:23,788 --> 00:35:24,913
You!

582
00:35:24,914 --> 00:35:27,083
Why are you here?

583
00:35:28,417 --> 00:35:29,709
You bowl cut!

584
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:32,796
I told you never to show
your face to me again!

585
00:35:32,797 --> 00:35:35,173
Witness, please calm down.

586
00:35:35,174 --> 00:35:37,510
Are you all in on this together?

587
00:35:38,094 --> 00:35:42,139
You set this up to watch me die of anger!

588
00:35:42,140 --> 00:35:45,601
Don't mess with me! You pieces of shit!

589
00:35:47,270 --> 00:35:50,189
Prosecutor, please escort the witness
out of the courtroom.

590
00:35:52,108 --> 00:35:54,734
You call me out here and then do this?

591
00:35:54,735 --> 00:35:57,154
Stop making a fool out of me!

592
00:35:57,155 --> 00:36:00,615
Why are you like this? Making a fool
of yourself in a place like this!

593
00:36:00,616 --> 00:36:02,659
Are you in on it, too?

594
00:36:02,660 --> 00:36:03,578
Let go of me!

595
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:07,248
We will recess for ten minutes.

596
00:36:11,794 --> 00:36:12,628
Are you alright?

597
00:36:18,509 --> 00:36:20,178
We will now resume.

598
00:36:32,106 --> 00:36:34,065
As you just saw,

599
00:36:34,066 --> 00:36:36,903
the victim is a difficult person
to live with.

600
00:36:38,070 --> 00:36:41,323
He becomes extremely suspicious
of his wife and berates her.

601
00:36:41,324 --> 00:36:43,867
Despite this, the defendant

602
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:45,577
supported her husband with dementia

603
00:36:45,578 --> 00:36:47,496
and cared for him devotedly.

604
00:36:48,497 --> 00:36:50,624
The defendant simply hit her husband

605
00:36:50,625 --> 00:36:52,250
impulsively out of sheer anger--

606
00:36:52,251 --> 00:36:53,585
Is something wrong?

607
00:36:53,586 --> 00:36:54,837
Over here.

608
00:37:03,179 --> 00:37:07,641
Your Honor, we have been informed
the victim died while being transported.

609
00:37:07,642 --> 00:37:09,560
W-- What did you just say?

610
00:37:10,061 --> 00:37:11,353
My husband?

611
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:13,439
My husband died...

612
00:37:15,608 --> 00:37:17,526
Therefore, we will consider

613
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:19,653
changing the charge in this case

614
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:22,198
from attempted murder to murder.

615
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:52,853
Incense offering is this way.

616
00:37:57,149 --> 00:37:58,567
Mr. Miyaji.

617
00:37:59,527 --> 00:38:02,112
Please accept my deepest condolences.

618
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:03,989
Thank you for coming all this way.

619
00:38:03,990 --> 00:38:05,074
Not at all.

620
00:38:06,867 --> 00:38:08,703
Thank you too, Minami.

621
00:38:12,873 --> 00:38:14,166
I...

622
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:18,587
I'm sorry.

623
00:38:20,006 --> 00:38:21,966
It is because I made him angry...

624
00:38:23,259 --> 00:38:24,885
It's not your fault, Minami.

625
00:38:26,012 --> 00:38:28,973
It's because of his rough temper.

626
00:38:30,558 --> 00:38:31,517
Besides...

627
00:38:32,518 --> 00:38:34,185
I'm the one...

628
00:38:34,186 --> 00:38:36,731
who swung that iron around.

629
00:38:39,859 --> 00:38:41,319
It's my fault.

630
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:46,324
I'm the one to blame.

631
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:04,716
FUNERAL VENUE
FOR THE LATE ISAO ICHINOSE

632
00:39:04,717 --> 00:39:06,719
It's unfortunate how things turned out.

633
00:39:08,512 --> 00:39:10,221
The responsibility is mine.

634
00:39:10,222 --> 00:39:12,641
Don't let it bother you, Ms. Minamida.

635
00:39:14,769 --> 00:39:18,229
With that said, I have decided

636
00:39:18,230 --> 00:39:21,650
to have Mr. Himi and Ms. Asahi
take over this case.

637
00:39:24,570 --> 00:39:26,238
You must still be processing it.

638
00:39:27,073 --> 00:39:28,532
You can take a few days off.

639
00:39:30,451 --> 00:39:32,620
Yes, I understand.

640
00:40:03,150 --> 00:40:07,279
<i>It seems you cannot
even see whales in the dark ocean.</i>

641
00:40:15,121 --> 00:40:15,954
I'm home.

642
00:40:15,955 --> 00:40:18,164
Welcome back, Minami.
You're hungry, right?

643
00:40:18,165 --> 00:40:19,791
We got some really good salt.

644
00:40:19,792 --> 00:40:22,253
Which ocean was it from? Minami?

645
00:40:33,347 --> 00:40:34,223
Can I?

646
00:40:40,521 --> 00:40:42,523
I thought you'd prefer your usual salt.

647
00:40:43,858 --> 00:40:45,943
Here you go, the Minami Minamida set.

648
00:40:46,735 --> 00:40:49,238
Being hungry keeps your mood down, too.

649
00:40:52,074 --> 00:40:54,452
Why did I become a lawyer?

650
00:40:56,078 --> 00:40:56,912
What's this now?

651
00:40:57,496 --> 00:41:00,040
My boss asked me that on my first day.

652
00:41:02,168 --> 00:41:03,252
I...

653
00:41:04,753 --> 00:41:06,714
I couldn't even answer that.

654
00:41:09,216 --> 00:41:10,801
Because I'm good at memorizing?

655
00:41:11,635 --> 00:41:13,179
Because I passed the bar?

656
00:41:15,306 --> 00:41:17,683
I remember everything I've ever read,

657
00:41:18,434 --> 00:41:20,019
but I can't ride an escalator alone.

658
00:41:23,272 --> 00:41:26,066
Maybe being a lawyer

659
00:41:26,775 --> 00:41:28,944
was impossible for me
with autism after all.

660
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:41,165
You know, Minami,

661
00:41:42,917 --> 00:41:45,044
any parent has at least one day

662
00:41:45,878 --> 00:41:49,381
where they think,
"Maybe my kid is special."

663
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:53,802
It's been almost 20 years now, I guess.

664
00:41:55,429 --> 00:41:56,639
I had...

665
00:41:57,306 --> 00:41:58,557
a day like that, too.

666
00:42:00,392 --> 00:42:01,268
Minami.

667
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:05,773
Minami Minamida.

668
00:42:09,568 --> 00:42:11,904
Most of the time when I talk to her,
she's like this.

669
00:42:12,988 --> 00:42:14,740
She hasn't spoken any words yet.

670
00:42:15,324 --> 00:42:17,952
Your daughter may have autism.

671
00:42:19,620 --> 00:42:21,413
Autism...

672
00:42:26,627 --> 00:42:27,753
<i>Hey, Minami.</i>

673
00:42:28,337 --> 00:42:31,048
Do you know who Dad is?

674
00:42:38,430 --> 00:42:39,515
Hey... Minami!

675
00:42:47,606 --> 00:42:48,523
Minami.

676
00:42:48,524 --> 00:42:51,025
- Hey, I've been waiting for you.
- H-- Hey, what is it?

677
00:42:51,026 --> 00:42:53,152
You! You made a move
on my wife, didn't you?

678
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:55,947
Hey, please stop! Hey!

679
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:58,700
What were you doing while I was out?

680
00:42:58,701 --> 00:43:01,202
What on earth were you doing with my wife?

681
00:43:01,203 --> 00:43:03,454
What on earth? My kid's watching! Stop it!

682
00:43:03,455 --> 00:43:05,124
What were you doing?

683
00:43:06,667 --> 00:43:08,586
Hey, what are you doing?

684
00:43:09,253 --> 00:43:10,212
Please, stop!

685
00:43:11,005 --> 00:43:12,213
I was working,

686
00:43:12,214 --> 00:43:14,257
so I just had your wife
look after my daughter.

687
00:43:14,258 --> 00:43:16,467
Looking at my wife with those pervy eyes.

688
00:43:16,468 --> 00:43:18,928
- You pervy four eyes!
- Please stop.

689
00:43:18,929 --> 00:43:20,681
- Hey!
- The crime of bodily injury.

690
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:25,184
A person who inflicts
bodily injury upon another

691
00:43:25,185 --> 00:43:29,732
shall face up to ten years in prison
or a 300,000 yen fine.

692
00:43:30,608 --> 00:43:31,442
Minami?

693
00:43:35,613 --> 00:43:36,779
Did you hear that?

694
00:43:36,780 --> 00:43:38,197
- You heard that, right?
- Yes!

695
00:43:38,198 --> 00:43:39,198
Minami spoke!

696
00:43:39,199 --> 00:43:40,367
"Crime of bodily injury!"

697
00:43:43,454 --> 00:43:44,830
Minami!

698
00:43:46,332 --> 00:43:47,333
You can speak.

699
00:43:48,292 --> 00:43:49,668
You can, Minami!

700
00:43:52,838 --> 00:43:54,840
Where did you learn that?

701
00:43:56,592 --> 00:43:57,634
Could it be...

702
00:43:57,635 --> 00:43:58,802
Wait here a second.

703
00:44:02,431 --> 00:44:05,017
Little Minami!

704
00:44:09,980 --> 00:44:12,065
Was it from here?

705
00:44:12,066 --> 00:44:13,525
The crime of bodily injury.

706
00:44:14,151 --> 00:44:15,902
A person who inflicts bodily injury

707
00:44:15,903 --> 00:44:19,697
upon another shall face up to ten years
in prison or a 300,000 yen fine.

708
00:44:19,698 --> 00:44:21,158
It all matches.

709
00:44:23,285 --> 00:44:24,827
Wonderful!

710
00:44:24,828 --> 00:44:26,871
She's a genius!

711
00:44:26,872 --> 00:44:29,624
That's why she's a little different
from other kids.

712
00:44:29,625 --> 00:44:34,755
Minami, you should become a lawyer
when you grow up.

713
00:44:35,673 --> 00:44:36,673
Yes!

714
00:44:36,674 --> 00:44:37,758
She will!

715
00:44:39,468 --> 00:44:40,678
The crime of bodily injury.

716
00:44:41,720 --> 00:44:42,887
Since then, Minami,

717
00:44:42,888 --> 00:44:45,808
you've stared at the
compendium of laws every day.

718
00:44:49,019 --> 00:44:51,146
COMPENDIUM OF LAWS

719
00:44:55,609 --> 00:44:59,780
So that was my motivation
for trying to become a lawyer.

720
00:45:00,864 --> 00:45:02,990
At that moment, I realized

721
00:45:02,991 --> 00:45:05,327
that you really had

722
00:45:05,869 --> 00:45:07,746
your own world inside you.

723
00:45:15,212 --> 00:45:16,296
Minami?

724
00:45:16,964 --> 00:45:18,173
Your rice balls?

725
00:45:27,057 --> 00:45:29,059
Go get 'em, Minami!

726
00:45:32,604 --> 00:45:34,522
Ms. Minamida,
did you forget something here?

727
00:45:34,523 --> 00:45:36,859
No, I didn't forget anything.

728
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:45,367
- Mr. Funai.
- Yes.

729
00:45:46,952 --> 00:45:48,578
The very first word I spoke

730
00:45:48,579 --> 00:45:51,248
when I was four
was "the crime of bodily injury."

731
00:45:51,832 --> 00:45:55,460
And the first person
who told me I should become a lawyer

732
00:45:55,461 --> 00:45:57,254
was Mr. Ichinose's wife.

733
00:45:58,005 --> 00:45:58,921
Right.

734
00:45:58,922 --> 00:46:00,799
I just found out and was surprised.

735
00:46:01,592 --> 00:46:05,219
And the first trial I'm in charge of
is for that same Keiko Ichinose.

736
00:46:05,220 --> 00:46:06,637
And the key to this trial

737
00:46:06,638 --> 00:46:10,100
is whether we can reduce her charge
to the crime of bodily injury.

738
00:46:10,809 --> 00:46:12,394
That's why I...

739
00:46:14,563 --> 00:46:16,772
In other words, are you saying you want

740
00:46:16,773 --> 00:46:18,817
to handle this case until the very end?

741
00:46:20,694 --> 00:46:21,903
Yes!

742
00:46:21,904 --> 00:46:24,656
I'm saying I want to handle
this case until the very end.

743
00:46:33,290 --> 00:46:34,124
Yes?

744
00:46:34,791 --> 00:46:35,709
Excuse me.

745
00:46:36,335 --> 00:46:38,294
The victim's death certificate arrived.

746
00:46:38,295 --> 00:46:39,963
You might want to take a look.

747
00:46:40,172 --> 00:46:41,465
Yes, I will take a look.

748
00:46:42,716 --> 00:46:44,550
DEATH CERTIFICATE

749
00:46:44,551 --> 00:46:47,888
Cause of death was indeed
a recurrence of the subdural hematoma.

750
00:46:54,228 --> 00:46:57,063
It's a miracle he didn't die instantly
after being hit

751
00:46:57,064 --> 00:46:58,482
on the head with this.

752
00:46:59,525 --> 00:47:01,108
Doesn't this iron look like that...

753
00:47:01,109 --> 00:47:02,902
- From <i>Pinocchio...</i>
- A sperm whale.

754
00:47:02,903 --> 00:47:04,571
Yes! A sperm whale.

755
00:47:05,405 --> 00:47:07,407
This part here looks like
the shape of its head.

756
00:47:12,788 --> 00:47:13,622
What is it?

757
00:47:18,043 --> 00:47:21,087
There are many things
I'm not allowed to do at work.

758
00:47:21,088 --> 00:47:23,089
Echolalia, weird remarks.

759
00:47:23,090 --> 00:47:25,132
Kayak, deed, rotator, civic, racecar.

760
00:47:25,133 --> 00:47:27,261
Also, speaking too honestly.

761
00:47:27,803 --> 00:47:28,636
Is that so?

762
00:47:28,637 --> 00:47:31,222
Especially talking about whales.
That's forbidden.

763
00:47:31,223 --> 00:47:32,683
Unless it's absolutely necessary.

764
00:47:33,350 --> 00:47:34,476
I'll be careful.

765
00:47:35,310 --> 00:47:37,938
Even if the iron looks like a sperm whale...

766
00:47:55,497 --> 00:47:58,624
Seeing the iron as a sperm whale

767
00:47:58,625 --> 00:48:00,918
made me miss that they don't lay eggs!

768
00:48:00,919 --> 00:48:01,962
What?

769
00:48:02,963 --> 00:48:06,132
In this case, civil law is relevant,
not criminal law.

770
00:48:06,133 --> 00:48:09,219
Likewise, we can't judge it
by the iron alone.

771
00:48:10,762 --> 00:48:11,638
The petition?

772
00:48:13,181 --> 00:48:14,224
The signature.

773
00:48:15,309 --> 00:48:17,060
Maybe there's an eyewitness.

774
00:48:18,562 --> 00:48:19,438
What?

775
00:48:22,941 --> 00:48:23,774
COURTHOUSE

776
00:48:23,775 --> 00:48:25,568
Let's proceed with cross-examination.

777
00:48:25,569 --> 00:48:26,944
3RD HEARING: WITNESS EXAMINATION

778
00:48:26,945 --> 00:48:28,030
Yes, Your Honor!

779
00:48:29,406 --> 00:48:33,534
Subdural hematomas include
traumatic ones caused by injuries

780
00:48:33,535 --> 00:48:36,287
and non-traumatic ones caused by illness.

781
00:48:36,288 --> 00:48:37,538
Is that correct?

782
00:48:37,539 --> 00:48:38,456
Yes.

783
00:48:38,457 --> 00:48:40,041
According to your diagnosis,

784
00:48:40,042 --> 00:48:42,460
the victim had no skull fractures

785
00:48:42,461 --> 00:48:44,378
and the head wound was shallow.

786
00:48:44,379 --> 00:48:45,379
Yes.

787
00:48:45,380 --> 00:48:47,423
Could the victim

788
00:48:47,424 --> 00:48:49,800
have had a non-traumatic subdural hematoma

789
00:48:49,801 --> 00:48:51,260
before the iron hit him?

790
00:48:51,261 --> 00:48:53,179
Before the iron hit him?

791
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:54,097
For instance...

792
00:48:56,892 --> 00:49:00,019
Exactly when the defendant swung the iron,

793
00:49:00,020 --> 00:49:03,606
the victim collapsed
due to a non-traumatic subdural hematoma.

794
00:49:03,607 --> 00:49:05,316
Is there no possibility of that?

795
00:49:05,317 --> 00:49:08,862
Objection. Counsel is seeking the
witness's opinion, not asking a question.

796
00:49:09,863 --> 00:49:11,072
Sustained.

797
00:49:11,073 --> 00:49:13,908
Defense, please only ask questions.

798
00:49:13,909 --> 00:49:15,117
Only ask questions.

799
00:49:15,118 --> 00:49:16,036
What?

800
00:49:29,424 --> 00:49:31,300
Mr. Isao was 81.

801
00:49:31,301 --> 00:49:33,552
He suffered from dementia.

802
00:49:33,553 --> 00:49:37,139
Non-traumatic subdural hematomas
are common in the elderly

803
00:49:37,140 --> 00:49:39,684
and dementia patients. Correct?

804
00:49:39,685 --> 00:49:40,810
Well,

805
00:49:40,811 --> 00:49:44,480
if there were warning signs or symptoms,
it would be a different story,

806
00:49:44,481 --> 00:49:48,235
but we can't confirm
a non-traumatic hematoma on that alone.

807
00:49:49,069 --> 00:49:52,405
It would be a different story
if there were warning signs?

808
00:49:52,406 --> 00:49:53,699
Well, yes.

809
00:50:00,706 --> 00:50:02,207
Thank you.

810
00:50:05,043 --> 00:50:06,961
Witness, you delivered a package

811
00:50:06,962 --> 00:50:10,173
to the Ichinose residence
on the day of the incident, correct?

812
00:50:10,424 --> 00:50:11,257
Yes.

813
00:50:11,258 --> 00:50:13,384
Who first answered the door

814
00:50:13,385 --> 00:50:15,387
when you delivered the package?

815
00:50:15,971 --> 00:50:17,764
Ms. Ichinose's husband.

816
00:50:20,100 --> 00:50:22,853
This is a copy of the delivery slip
from that time.

817
00:50:28,191 --> 00:50:30,610
Whose signature is this
in the receipt section?

818
00:50:31,194 --> 00:50:32,571
Ms. Ichinose.

819
00:50:36,283 --> 00:50:38,702
Why didn't you get Mr. Isao's signature?

820
00:50:39,411 --> 00:50:41,163
I tried to, but...

821
00:50:43,039 --> 00:50:44,874
My head feels like it's splitting.

822
00:50:44,875 --> 00:50:47,084
Package here. Can I get a signature?

823
00:50:47,085 --> 00:50:48,086
Yeah.

824
00:50:51,882 --> 00:50:53,383
My fingers are numb.

825
00:50:54,301 --> 00:50:56,385
- Are you okay?
- Shut up!

826
00:50:56,386 --> 00:50:58,805
Hey, a package arrived.

827
00:50:59,306 --> 00:51:00,891
You sign for it.

828
00:51:05,604 --> 00:51:06,729
Looking at the slip,

829
00:51:06,730 --> 00:51:11,026
there's a messy line here
protruding from the signature box.

830
00:51:12,652 --> 00:51:16,822
There's no doubt that this was written
by her husband, Mr. Isao,

831
00:51:16,823 --> 00:51:19,284
when he tried to sign, correct?

832
00:51:20,535 --> 00:51:22,369
Objection! Leading the witness.

833
00:51:22,370 --> 00:51:23,496
Overruled.

834
00:51:23,497 --> 00:51:25,332
Witness, what is your answer?

835
00:51:31,463 --> 00:51:32,839
That's correct.

836
00:51:36,468 --> 00:51:37,427
Your Honor!

837
00:51:38,136 --> 00:51:41,347
Before the incident,
the victim had numbness in his fingertips

838
00:51:41,348 --> 00:51:43,307
and couldn't even write a signature.

839
00:51:43,308 --> 00:51:45,519
Furthermore, he complained of a headache.

840
00:51:46,228 --> 00:51:49,815
These can be called warning signs
of a non-traumatic subdural hematoma.

841
00:51:50,524 --> 00:51:53,400
In other words, the subdural hematoma

842
00:51:53,401 --> 00:51:56,070
may not have been caused
by the defendant's assault,

843
00:51:56,071 --> 00:51:58,531
but by his pre-existing illness!

844
00:51:58,532 --> 00:52:00,408
I'll kill you...

845
00:52:01,493 --> 00:52:03,536
And then I'll die too!

846
00:52:03,537 --> 00:52:05,372
This is the end.

847
00:52:09,584 --> 00:52:12,211
In criminal trials,
there is a fundamental principle

848
00:52:12,212 --> 00:52:15,006
that the defendant gets
the benefit of the doubt.

849
00:52:15,799 --> 00:52:19,593
Since his pre-existing illness
may have caused his death...

850
00:52:19,594 --> 00:52:21,554
Unless the prosecution

851
00:52:21,555 --> 00:52:23,889
can medically prove a causal relationship

852
00:52:23,890 --> 00:52:26,977
between the defendant's strike
and the resulting death...

853
00:52:28,144 --> 00:52:30,104
The defendant cannot be held

854
00:52:30,105 --> 00:52:32,774
criminally responsible
for the death itself!

855
00:52:37,445 --> 00:52:41,533
It seems we will need
to re-examine this matter.

856
00:52:52,002 --> 00:52:53,295
That is all.

857
00:53:04,806 --> 00:53:07,141
It depends on the prosecution's proof,

858
00:53:07,142 --> 00:53:10,395
but you'll likely get
a suspended sentence for bodily injury.

859
00:53:11,396 --> 00:53:12,981
Thank you.

860
00:53:17,569 --> 00:53:18,820
Ms. Minamida.

861
00:53:20,155 --> 00:53:21,156
You did a good job.

862
00:53:22,574 --> 00:53:24,034
Yes. I did a good job.

863
00:53:27,329 --> 00:53:28,455
Ms. Minamida.

864
00:53:31,249 --> 00:53:32,584
It's all thanks to you.

865
00:53:34,461 --> 00:53:36,338
Thank you so much.

866
00:53:41,760 --> 00:53:43,219
Thank you.

867
00:54:16,544 --> 00:54:17,963
Thank you very much.

868
00:54:18,421 --> 00:54:19,381
What?

869
00:54:20,423 --> 00:54:23,008
Thanks to you thinking it through with me,

870
00:54:23,009 --> 00:54:25,929
I realized the iron
didn't cause a fatal wound.

871
00:54:26,763 --> 00:54:29,808
It's all thanks to you.
You fought for your client.

872
00:54:32,352 --> 00:54:33,603
About that thing...

873
00:54:34,938 --> 00:54:36,063
That thing?

874
00:54:36,064 --> 00:54:37,439
Talking about whales.

875
00:54:37,440 --> 00:54:39,859
Isn't it fine
when it's just the two of us?

876
00:54:41,152 --> 00:54:42,028
What?

877
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:44,656
Is it really okay?

878
00:54:45,156 --> 00:54:46,491
I don't mind.

879
00:54:47,492 --> 00:54:49,284
To talk about whales?

880
00:54:49,285 --> 00:54:50,662
Yes.

881
00:54:52,497 --> 00:54:54,748
When it's just you and me, Mr. Funai?

882
00:54:54,749 --> 00:54:57,168
Yeah. When it's just the two of us.

883
00:55:02,632 --> 00:55:03,967
Thank you!

884
00:55:08,763 --> 00:55:09,806
Are you okay?

885
00:55:11,057 --> 00:55:13,643
I don't know where to start.

886
00:55:14,728 --> 00:55:17,272
First, let's talk about sperm whales!

887
00:55:18,189 --> 00:55:19,024
Okay.

888
00:55:21,109 --> 00:55:22,943
Most female sperm whales

889
00:55:22,944 --> 00:55:25,279
spend their entire lives in the same pod.

890
00:55:25,280 --> 00:55:27,781
Males leave the pod around age ten

891
00:55:27,782 --> 00:55:30,784
and form pods
with other young adult males.

892
00:55:30,785 --> 00:55:33,913
As they mature further,
they begin to travel alone.

893
00:55:43,173 --> 00:55:45,008
Sorry. We're closed for today--

894
00:55:50,013 --> 00:55:50,972
Long time no see.

895
00:56:03,651 --> 00:56:05,736
Her wedding dress slipped down

896
00:56:05,737 --> 00:56:07,446
during the ceremony...

897
00:56:07,447 --> 00:56:09,406
How much do you think that ceremony cost?

898
00:56:09,407 --> 00:56:10,950
The husband loves his wife--

899
00:56:11,743 --> 00:56:13,911
Let's go undercover for this one.

900
00:56:13,912 --> 00:56:16,872
My, my, the groom
is completely captivated.

901
00:56:16,873 --> 00:56:17,832
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
